  "representative_html_projection": "<main><div><h1 id=\"learn-nodejs\"><a href=\"#learn-nodejs\" class=\"anchor\">Learn Node.js</a></h1></div> <p>Welcome to the Node.js learning resources. Whether you're just getting started or looking to deepen your knowledge, these guides cover everything from the basics to advanced topics.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"/learn/getting-started/introduction-to-nodejs\">Getting Started</a> — Install Node.js and write your first program</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/command-line/run-nodejs-scripts-from-the-command-line\">Command Line</a> — Run scripts, use the REPL, and handle I/O</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/http/anatomy-of-an-http-transaction\">HTTP</a> — Build web servers and work with HTTP</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/manipulating-files/nodejs-file-stats\">File System</a> — Read, write, and manipulate files</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/asynchronous-work/javascript-asynchronous-programming-and-callbacks\">Asynchronous Work</a> — Understand async patterns, promises, and the event loop</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/concurrency/comparing-nodejs-concurrency-models\">Concurrency</a> — Compare child processes, worker threads, and cluster</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/typescript/introduction\">TypeScript</a> — Use TypeScript with Node.js</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/getting-started/an-introduction-to-the-npm-package-manager\">Package Management</a> — Publish and manage packages</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/diagnostics/user-journey\">Diagnostics</a> — Debug performance and memory issues</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/test-runner/introduction\">Testing</a> — Write and run tests with the built-in test runner</li> <li><a href=\"/learn/getting-started/security-best-practices\">Security</a> — Follow security best practices</li> </ul></main>",
